  "summary": "I added a \"Pause flythrough\" button below the canvas and a `window.__TASK_STATE__` object. Typecheck passes and the render shows no errors, with the canvas still animating. I didn't click the button or read `__TASK_STATE__` in the browser, so pause, resume and the state values are untested.\n\n- **Button:** it is a DOM button in index.html, wired up in src/main.ts. Clicking it stops the camera where it is while the scene keeps rendering. The label switches to \"Resume flythrough\", and clicking again continues from the same spot.\n- **Camera time:** the flythrough now runs on its own clock that only advances while flying, instead of the frame timer. Pausing therefore freezes the camera position, and resuming carries on without a jump.\n- **State object:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` holds `flying`, `cameraX`, `cameraY` and `cameraZ`, updated every frame. It reflects the camera position the code computes for that frame, not one read back from the renderer.\n\nThe screenshot shows the button under the canvas, labelled \"Pause flythrough\"."
